course: dictionary
lesson: 8836
title: Ship: a noun and a verb
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one job in a sentence. Ship can be a thing, or it can be a doing word. The words around it are its context, and they show you which one it is. «The ship sailed into the harbour at dawn.» Here a ship is a thing, a big boat that carries people or goods across the sea.
explain: «The shop will ship the boots to our house on Friday.» Now ship is a doing word, and it means to send goods by sea, road, air or post. Ask: what word would fit here? Try the word send in the sentence instead. If it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Shipping is a noun that comes from the same word. «The shipping cost was high, so we did not buy the lamp.» Shipping can mean the sending of goods, or the money you pay to have them sent. The clue is the word cost, so here it means the money.
fact: Ship is a noun and a verb: a ship is a big boat, and to ship is to send goods.
fact: A spaceship is a vehicle that travels in space.
fact: Shipping means sending goods, or the cost of sending them.
fact: Most goods now cross the sea in standard steel boxes on giant ships.
fact: Charles Darwin sailed around the world on the ship Beagle, and he filled notebooks on the voyage.
exercise: «The ship sailed into the harbour at dawn.» What is a ship in this sentence? | To send goods by post | A line painted on the side of a boat | A shop that sells boots | *A big boat that carries people or goods across the sea
exercise: «The shop will ship the boots to our house on Friday.» What does ship mean here? | *To send goods | To count boxes in maths | To travel into space | To sail on a big boat
exercise: Ahmed says a spaceship is a boat that sails on the sea. What is a spaceship? | A kind of cloud | *A vehicle that travels in space | A giant steel box | A boat that sails on the sea
test: «The shipping cost was high, so we did not buy the lamp.» What does shipping mean here? | *The cost of sending goods | Shiny and new | A party for sailors | A big boat on the sea
test: «Charles Darwin filled notebooks on his voyage on the ship Beagle.» What kind of thing was the Beagle? | A spaceship | A farm animal | *A big boat that carried people across the sea | A type of notebook
exam: «Farmers dry the beans in the sun before they are shipped.» What does shipped mean here? | *Sent away to buyers as goods | Scooped out of the pods | Cut from the pods | Left to ferment under leaves
